00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.820
What separates blackjack
from other games


00:03:52.863 --> 00:03:55.736
is that it's based on
dependent events,


00:03:55.779 --> 00:03:59.478
meaning past affects
the probability in the future.


00:03:59.522 --> 00:04:02.438
The house has a 1.5% advantage.


00:04:03.831 --> 00:04:06.007
If a player knows the nature
of the cards in the shoe,


00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.400
he can turn the house advantage
to himself.


00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.969
To do this, he has to


00:04:12.013 --> 00:04:14.102
keep track of every card
that is played.


00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.670
Count is based on
a high/low system.


00:04:17.714 --> 00:04:20.238
High cards--
ten, jack, queen, king--


00:04:20.282 --> 00:04:22.327
have a value of minus-one.


00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:26.288
If they are depleted,
player's advantage goes down.


00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.944
The low cards--
two, three, four, five, six--


00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:32.076
have a value of plus-one.


00:04:34.905 --> 00:04:38.213
The seven, eight and nine
have no count value.


00:04:38.256 --> 00:04:39.997
The player keeps track
of every card


00:04:40.041 --> 00:04:42.783
and calculates
the running count.


00:04:42.826 --> 00:04:44.828
Then the player arrives
at the true count,


00:04:44.872 --> 00:04:47.657
which is the running count
divided by the decks remaining.


00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.790
For example, if the
running count is plus-nine


00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.096
and there are four and a half
decks remaining,


00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.447
nine over four and a half gives
you a true count of plus-two.


00:04:56.884 --> 00:04:58.407
As true count increases,


00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.626
the player's advantage
increases.


00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:04.456
The idea is to bet little when
you don't have the advantage,


00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.676
more when you do.


