00:42:10.637 --> 00:42:12.595
It stores it all.


00:42:14.597 --> 00:42:16.556
Do you want to hear about it?


00:42:16.599 --> 00:42:18.471
Would that interest you?


00:42:19.559 --> 00:42:21.604
-What?
-You know what.


00:42:21.648 --> 00:42:23.737
You're dying to hear.


00:42:34.182 --> 00:42:36.445
The noise.


00:42:38.056 --> 00:42:40.058
The smell.


00:42:41.363 --> 00:42:45.019
Feces, urine,


00:42:45.063 --> 00:42:47.761
oil, explosives,


00:42:47.804 --> 00:42:51.199
bleach, sweat, smoke.


00:42:51.243 --> 00:42:54.072
All day, every day.


00:42:54.115 --> 00:42:56.074
Sand spiders, camel spiders,


00:42:56.117 --> 00:42:58.380
ants as big as cockroaches.


00:42:58.424 --> 00:43:01.035
The heat, the fear,


00:43:01.079 --> 00:43:03.298
the adrenaline jack, mortars.


00:43:03.342 --> 00:43:05.039
The sheer noise of it.


00:43:05.083 --> 00:43:07.433
And blood.


00:43:07.476 --> 00:43:10.827
And the only way to survive
was to rise above.


00:43:10.871 --> 00:43:12.786
Rise and laugh.


00:43:12.829 --> 00:43:15.310
Surf the craziness.


00:43:15.354 --> 00:43:18.879
To see a grown man shit
and piss on himself.


00:43:20.141 --> 00:43:21.664
Sing the song, man.


00:43:21.708 --> 00:43:24.363
The noise, the fucking noise.


00:43:26.452 --> 00:43:28.236
The noise.


00:43:29.411 --> 00:43:31.152
We were all just trapped
in there,


00:43:31.196 --> 00:43:35.591
in the same shit,
sh-sh... shithole.


00:43:37.811 --> 00:43:39.726
Them and us.


00:43:42.903 --> 00:43:45.862
And am I trying to justify
what we did?


00:43:49.214 --> 00:43:50.954
No.


00:43:54.784 --> 00:43:56.612
Nothing...


00:43:58.223 --> 00:44:01.400
Nothing can justify
what we did.


00:44:04.838 --> 00:44:07.014
Your father understood that.


00:44:08.755 --> 00:44:11.192
If you were there,
you could understand.


00:44:12.237 --> 00:44:15.327
Otherwise, there's no...


00:44:15.370 --> 00:44:17.416
understanding.


00:44:49.361 --> 00:44:51.363
Minnesota?


00:44:55.758 --> 00:44:57.760
When was the last time?


00:44:57.804 --> 00:44:59.501
Orlando?


00:44:59.545 --> 00:45:01.242
Oxford Downs. That's right.


00:45:01.286 --> 00:45:03.113
-You were with Clickity Dick.
-USA! USA!


00:45:03.157 --> 00:45:05.246
I'd like to put a cap
in that motherfucker.


00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:07.466
-Now, take it smooth, Minnie.


00:45:07.509 --> 00:45:10.556
-And exercise those legs.


00:45:14.168 --> 00:45:16.170
They call him Minnesota Fats
after the movie.


00:45:16.214 --> 00:45:17.998
You know, there's not
a lot of fat people


00:45:18.041 --> 00:45:20.000
that play
professional poker anymore.


00:45:20.043 --> 00:45:22.263
I like to call him
Charlie Two Chins.


00:45:22.307 --> 00:45:23.917
Why is that?


00:45:23.960 --> 00:45:25.962
'Cause he got more chins
than a Chinese phone book.


00:45:26.006 --> 00:45:27.877
Thanks for the straight line.


00:45:27.921 --> 00:45:29.705
Minnesota Fats played pool
in that movie.


00:45:29.749 --> 00:45:31.751
-No, poker.
-No, that's Cincinnati Kid.


00:45:31.794 --> 00:45:33.579
Oh, whatever.


00:45:42.631 --> 00:45:44.416
The preferred poker variant


00:45:44.459 --> 00:45:47.941
for multi-table tournaments
is no-limit Texas Hold'em.


00:45:47.984 --> 00:45:50.944
It encourages large pots
and large raises.


00:45:50.987 --> 00:45:54.252
The prize money is split
between the top five players.


00:45:55.644 --> 00:45:57.342
Before the hole cards are dealt,


00:45:57.385 --> 00:46:00.083
the player to the left
of the button must post


00:46:00.127 --> 00:46:01.607
small and big blinds.


00:46:03.130 --> 00:46:06.786
This stimulates action, and
the blinds go up every hour.


00:46:13.140 --> 00:46:15.403
The rest of the cards
are common cards.


00:46:19.059 --> 00:46:21.148
The flop, three cards.


00:46:31.985 --> 00:46:33.639
1,800.


00:46:47.653 --> 00:46:49.872
The turn.


00:47:08.630 --> 00:47:10.850
And the river.


00:47:10.893 --> 00:47:13.983
The river can instantly turn
a losing hand into a winner.


00:47:14.027 --> 00:47:16.551
That's Hold'em's
betting appeal.


00:47:16.595 --> 00:47:18.031
All in.


00:47:50.455 --> 00:47:52.631
What happened? You get bored?


00:47:52.674 --> 00:47:54.589
Played some slots.


00:47:54.633 --> 00:47:56.852
You should read some books.


00:47:56.896 --> 00:47:58.419
I'm gonna buy you one.


00:47:58.463 --> 00:48:00.073
I've read books.


00:48:00.116 --> 00:48:01.509
What is it with her?


00:48:01.553 --> 00:48:03.119
-Name one.
-One what?


00:48:03.163 --> 00:48:04.991
Book.


00:48:05.034 --> 00:48:06.906
How 'bout Poker for Dummies.


00:48:06.949 --> 00:48:08.560
I believe you may have read it.


00:48:08.603 --> 00:48:10.779
I like him.


00:48:13.478 --> 00:48:16.132
Wow. You made it
to the second dinner break.


00:48:16.176 --> 00:48:19.353
I must have fired
two dozen tournaments


00:48:19.397 --> 00:48:21.790
before I lasted that long.


00:48:21.834 --> 00:48:24.402
So, how many are left?


00:48:24.445 --> 00:48:27.317
Four tables,
so should be done tomorrow.


00:48:28.580 --> 00:48:30.669
How much cards do you play?


00:48:33.715 --> 00:48:35.761
40 hands an hour,


00:48:35.804 --> 00:48:38.590
eight to 12 hours a day,
six to seven days a week.


00:48:38.633 --> 00:48:40.766
Do you do anything else?


00:48:40.809 --> 00:48:42.420
Like what?


00:48:42.463 --> 00:48:43.943
Like anything.


00:48:43.986 --> 00:48:47.207
Go to a park,
a concert, a museum.


00:48:47.250 --> 00:48:49.035
-Museum?
-Yeah.


00:48:49.078 --> 00:48:50.863
I'll buy you a book on it.
It's called...


00:48:50.906 --> 00:48:52.430
Museums for Dummies.


00:48:52.473 --> 00:48:55.128
Ba-dum-bum.


00:48:55.171 --> 00:48:58.610
No, but seriously,
you should do something else.


00:48:58.653 --> 00:49:00.612
Just for variety.


00:49:05.007 --> 00:49:07.096
I like playing cards.


00:49:23.983 --> 00:49:26.159
USA!


00:49:26.202 --> 00:49:29.292
USA! USA! USA!


00:49:36.386 --> 00:49:38.824
That's $800,000.


00:49:38.867 --> 00:49:40.521
Where do they get their money?


00:49:40.565 --> 00:49:42.392
Geez Louise.


00:49:42.436 --> 00:49:43.916
Slow down, Kid.


00:49:43.959 --> 00:49:46.266
You see the purple chips?
What do they say?


00:49:46.309 --> 00:49:47.920
5,000.


00:49:47.963 --> 00:49:49.530
5,000 what?


00:49:49.574 --> 00:49:51.401
5,000 grains of rice?


00:49:51.445 --> 00:49:53.012
That's not money.


00:49:53.055 --> 00:49:54.666
Those are tournament chips.


00:49:54.709 --> 00:49:56.232
We just call them dollars.


00:49:56.276 --> 00:49:57.843
It's good publicity.


00:49:57.886 --> 00:49:59.932
So, how much is it?


00:49:59.975 --> 00:50:03.109
Depends on the buy-in
and the split.


00:50:03.152 --> 00:50:07.026
A game like this,
there's about 500,000 in play.


00:50:07.069 --> 00:50:09.550
The winner will get 150,


00:50:09.594 --> 00:50:13.293
runner-up anywhere 70 to 80,
and so on.


00:50:13.336 --> 00:50:16.688
-- Oh, yeah!
-- USA! USA!


00:50:16.731 --> 00:50:20.866
USA! USA! USA!


00:50:20.909 --> 00:50:22.737
You know who he is?


00:50:22.781 --> 00:50:24.173
Who?


00:50:24.217 --> 00:50:27.002
Bill Tell or whatever
his real name is.


00:50:27.046 --> 00:50:28.961
You know who he is, right?


00:50:29.004 --> 00:50:32.094
All I've ever heard was
William Tell.


00:50:32.138 --> 00:50:34.096
Why do you think
he has another name?


00:50:34.140 --> 00:50:36.142
You've been around him.


00:50:36.185 --> 00:50:38.361
He's a mystery.


00:50:38.405 --> 00:50:41.451
And I don't know if that's
a good thing or a bad thing.


00:50:41.495 --> 00:50:43.671
Am I in any danger?


00:50:43.715 --> 00:50:45.064
Of what?


00:50:45.107 --> 00:50:46.718
Falling in love?


00:50:46.761 --> 00:50:49.634
Don't be a child.


00:50:49.677 --> 00:50:51.679
What is his past?


00:50:51.723 --> 00:50:53.594
I haven't asked.


00:50:53.638 --> 00:50:55.553
Well, what are you two
doing together?


00:50:55.596 --> 00:50:57.206
I don't have any goals.


00:50:57.250 --> 00:51:00.122
I'm just along for the ride,
one day at a time.


00:51:00.166 --> 00:51:01.907
Hmm.


00:51:03.822 --> 00:51:06.085
What do you think
he's holding?


00:51:06.128 --> 00:51:08.914
I don't know, but if
you be quiet, we'll find out.


00:51:11.612 --> 00:51:13.440
All in.


00:51:18.967 --> 00:51:20.882
Call.


00:51:25.757 --> 00:51:28.629
Oh, yeah! USA!


00:51:28.673 --> 00:51:31.240
USA! USA!


00:51:31.284 --> 00:51:34.896
-USA! USA!


00:51:36.768 --> 00:51:39.901
-USA!
-That's it, baby.


00:51:45.733 --> 00:51:47.909
All right.


00:51:47.953 --> 00:51:50.129
54,000 for a night's work.


00:51:50.172 --> 00:51:52.392
Hope you're not disappointed.


00:51:52.435 --> 00:51:56.178
That's, uh, 27 for you,
27 for me.


00:51:56.222 --> 00:51:58.572
Let me sign this.


00:51:58.616 --> 00:52:00.574
Hey, uh, excuse me a second.


00:52:00.618 --> 00:52:01.967
Got to hose it.


00:52:02.010 --> 00:52:03.490
All right.


00:52:03.533 --> 00:52:05.535
I'll have a Manhattan.


00:52:05.579 --> 00:52:08.190
I'll have the, uh...
the same, please.


00:52:09.975 --> 00:52:12.455
Here you go.


00:52:12.499 --> 00:52:14.544
Thanks.


00:52:21.726 --> 00:52:23.423
Thank you.


00:52:24.685 --> 00:52:27.340
-Cheers.
-Cheers.


00:52:34.477 --> 00:52:37.567
What did you mean when
you said that the other day?


00:52:38.525 --> 00:52:40.266
Said what?


00:52:40.309 --> 00:52:41.876
I woke you.


00:52:41.920 --> 00:52:43.486
What does that mean?


00:52:46.141 --> 00:52:48.796
I don't know.
It was just something I said.


00:52:48.840 --> 00:52:50.580
It's just a comment.


00:52:50.624 --> 00:52:52.670
Mm.


00:52:52.713 --> 00:52:54.715
It's a odd thing to say.


00:52:57.065 --> 00:52:59.851
So, what's your story?


00:52:59.894 --> 00:53:02.505
Everybody's got a story.


00:53:02.549 --> 00:53:04.638
What's yourstory?


00:53:07.162 --> 00:53:09.774
Why poker?


00:53:09.817 --> 00:53:12.211
Let me guess-- it has
something to do with a man.


00:53:12.254 --> 00:53:14.430
-Bingo.
-Where was this?


00:53:15.823 --> 00:53:17.520
East Saint Louis.


00:53:17.564 --> 00:53:19.392
He went outside his zone.


00:53:19.435 --> 00:53:20.654
He tilted.


00:53:20.698 --> 00:53:21.742
Which direction?


00:53:21.786 --> 00:53:23.483
Violence.


00:53:23.526 --> 00:53:26.007
But he had some good friends
who liked me,


00:53:26.051 --> 00:53:28.706
and they were gamblers,


00:53:28.749 --> 00:53:31.317
and I drifted
in that direction.


00:53:31.360 --> 00:53:35.364
And... they said I have
very good people skills.


00:53:36.757 --> 00:53:39.542
Yeah, I found something
I'm good at.


00:53:42.589 --> 00:53:44.460
I like you.


00:53:48.464 --> 00:53:51.380
I like this friendship we have.


00:54:01.347 --> 00:54:03.305
So, um...


00:54:03.349 --> 00:54:05.351
what are your plans?


00:54:05.394 --> 00:54:07.832
I like, uh...
I like where it's headed.


00:54:07.875 --> 00:54:09.442
I mean tonight.


00:54:12.314 --> 00:54:14.099
I got to go back to my motel.


00:54:14.142 --> 00:54:15.927
I got some work to do.


00:54:15.970 --> 00:54:18.712
You're not staying here?


00:54:18.756 --> 00:54:20.670
No, I don't like staying
at casinos.


00:54:20.714 --> 00:54:23.238
They know everything about
you-- the maids and the staff.


00:54:23.282 --> 00:54:24.631
Corridor cameras, noise.


00:54:24.674 --> 00:54:26.633
It's not for me.


00:54:26.676 --> 00:54:28.461
See you down the road,
La Linda.


00:54:30.898 --> 00:54:32.334
Cleveland, right?


00:54:32.378 --> 00:54:34.423
Yeah.


00:55:01.233 --> 00:55:04.540
His real name was John Rodgers.


00:55:04.584 --> 00:55:07.717
"John Gordo" came
sometime later.


00:55:07.761 --> 00:55:09.719
He was born in Georgia.


00:55:09.763 --> 00:55:11.809
He first came to the attention
of the CIA


00:55:11.852 --> 00:55:14.376
during the Contra
counterinsurgency.


00:55:15.987 --> 00:55:18.903
He was trained in interrogation
in Nicaragua.


00:55:20.034 --> 00:55:21.862
From there, he entered
the SERE program.


00:55:21.906 --> 00:55:24.865
Survival, Evasion,
Resistance and Escape.


00:55:26.432 --> 00:55:28.913
The program was devised
to help captured U.S. soldiers


00:55:28.956 --> 00:55:31.306
withstand hostile
interrogations.


00:55:31.350 --> 00:55:33.221
Get the fuck up! Get up!


00:55:38.879 --> 00:55:41.839
They were put
into stress conditions.


00:55:42.883 --> 00:55:45.277
Sensory deprivation,


00:55:45.320 --> 00:55:47.888
confinement in close spaces,


00:55:47.932 --> 00:55:51.065
given bombardment with
dangerous decibels of noise.


00:55:54.155 --> 00:55:57.811
Starvation, sleep deprivation.


00:56:00.553 --> 00:56:02.207
And sexual humiliation.


00:56:18.353 --> 00:56:20.703
After the foreign fighters at
the Guantanamo detention camp


00:56:20.747 --> 00:56:23.793
were unresponsive
to interrogations,


00:56:23.837 --> 00:56:26.492
a decision was made
to reverse engineer


00:56:26.535 --> 00:56:28.189
the lessons learned
in the SERE program.


00:56:30.931 --> 00:56:33.325
SERE psych op instructors
were brought to Gitmo


00:56:33.368 --> 00:56:36.502
to devise enhanced
interrogation techniques.


00:56:37.982 --> 00:56:40.071
One of the first to arrive


00:56:40.114 --> 00:56:44.466
was consultant John Gordo,
now a civilian.


00:56:44.510 --> 00:56:46.599
Lessons learned at Gitmo
were conveyed


00:56:46.642 --> 00:56:49.080
to interrogation black sites
around the world.


00:56:53.127 --> 00:56:55.477
In 2003, a decision was made


00:56:55.521 --> 00:56:57.740
to Gitmo-ize
the civilian prisons


00:56:57.784 --> 00:57:00.352
at Bagram Airfield
and Abu Ghraib.


00:57:03.094 --> 00:57:06.836
Civilian consultant John Gordo
arrived in May.


00:57:10.928 --> 00:57:12.842
Did you go to college, Tillich?


00:57:12.886 --> 00:57:14.801
Community college, two years.


00:57:14.844 --> 00:57:16.803
They teach you
creativity there?


00:57:16.846 --> 00:57:18.109
No, sir.


00:57:18.152 --> 00:57:19.849
Well, that's what
it takes here.


00:57:19.893 --> 00:57:21.286
Not everything's
black-and-white.


00:57:21.329 --> 00:57:22.765
You got to use
your imagination.


00:57:22.809 --> 00:57:25.420
This isn't about
following a manual.


00:57:25.464 --> 00:57:27.379
It's about getting answers.


00:57:27.422 --> 00:57:29.381
Answers that'll save
American lives.


00:57:29.424 --> 00:57:31.165
What if they don't know
the answers?


00:57:31.209 --> 00:57:33.124
They all say that.


00:57:33.167 --> 00:57:34.995
That's their culture.


00:57:35.039 --> 00:57:36.954
Follow me.


00:57:36.997 --> 00:57:38.694
Wake him up!


00:57:38.738 --> 00:57:41.523
Baufort, get in there.


00:57:41.567 --> 00:57:43.786
Time to talk, little buddy.


00:57:43.830 --> 00:57:46.572
-Up! Let's go!


00:57:49.401 --> 00:57:51.403
Go!


00:57:51.446 --> 00:57:53.405
-I'll be right back.


00:57:53.448 --> 00:57:54.972
Tillich...


00:57:55.015 --> 00:57:57.061
I like you.


00:57:57.104 --> 00:57:59.324
I think you got what it takes.


00:57:59.367 --> 00:58:01.674
You got the right stuff.


00:58:01.717 --> 00:58:04.372
I'm gonna put you
on night shift.


00:58:04.416 --> 00:58:07.897
That's where all
the good stuff happens.


00:58:07.941 --> 00:58:11.292
Okay, let's fuck this Ahmed up!


00:58:12.511 --> 00:58:15.557
Greer. Wipe that shit
off of him.


00:58:15.601 --> 00:58:18.865
Your easy days are over, Ahmed.


00:58:18.908 --> 00:58:20.388
Come on.


00:58:20.432 --> 00:58:22.434
Get him up. Get him up.


00:58:25.741 --> 00:58:27.395
Gordo was right.


00:58:28.657 --> 00:58:30.703
I had it in me.


00:58:33.619 --> 00:58:35.925
I had the right stuff.


00:58:55.771 --> 00:58:57.730
The Kid was right.


00:58:57.773 --> 00:59:00.994
When those photos came out,
Gordo vanished.


00:59:04.737 --> 00:59:08.697
The only ones prosecuted
were in the pictures.


00:59:08.741 --> 00:59:10.612
Not their superiors.


00:59:10.656 --> 00:59:13.833
Not their superiors' superiors.


00:59:13.876 --> 00:59:17.837
Gordo moved on, started
his own consulting company.


00:59:17.880 --> 00:59:20.405
I heard he was
working in Cairo.


00:59:22.581 --> 00:59:26.106
In the military,
rank means everything.


00:59:26.150 --> 00:59:29.544
In USDB, it means nothing.


00:59:31.503 --> 00:59:32.852
The f...


00:59:32.895 --> 00:59:34.288
-What you doing, man?
-What?


00:59:34.332 --> 00:59:35.724
-You got a problem?
-No. I'm sorry.


00:59:35.768 --> 00:59:37.944
-You got a problem?
-I'm sorry.


00:59:37.987 --> 00:59:40.033
Sorry about that.


01:00:02.795 --> 01:00:05.493
Do it. Do it.


01:00:15.938 --> 01:00:17.940
Bitch.


01:00:25.731 --> 01:00:29.561
Prisoner's name
was Clay Williams.


01:00:29.604 --> 01:00:32.172
I don't know if he's
alive or dead.


01:00:32.216 --> 01:00:34.000
If he were alive,


01:00:34.043 --> 01:00:36.916
I wonder if I could hire him
to finish the job.


01:00:44.053 --> 01:00:46.795
You know,
this ain't such a bad life.


01:00:46.839 --> 01:00:48.884
I think I could
get used to this.


01:00:50.669 --> 01:00:52.410
It's a thin margin.


01:00:52.453 --> 01:00:54.368
It's 24-7.


01:00:54.412 --> 01:00:56.501
Most cats can't cut it.


01:00:59.243 --> 01:01:01.114
So, how'd you meet La Linda?


01:01:01.158 --> 01:01:02.463
I like her.


01:01:02.507 --> 01:01:04.465
She runs a stable.


01:01:04.509 --> 01:01:06.293
That's what they call
a group of gamblers


01:01:06.337 --> 01:01:07.729
backed by investors.


01:01:07.773 --> 01:01:09.383
The gamblers are the horses.


01:01:09.427 --> 01:01:11.037
The investors put up the money.


01:01:11.080 --> 01:01:13.692
Split the winnings
with the, uh... the stable.


01:01:14.997 --> 01:01:17.478
But why don't they just
use their own money?


01:01:19.176 --> 01:01:20.916
OPM.


01:01:22.570 --> 01:01:24.790
Other people's money.


01:01:24.833 --> 01:01:28.663
Casino, the TV, the websites--
they all want big pots.


01:01:28.707 --> 01:01:30.796
It's entertainment.


01:01:34.147 --> 01:01:36.018
Hey, where are we going, anyway?


01:01:36.062 --> 01:01:37.803
I thought Saint Louis
was back that way.


01:01:37.846 --> 01:01:39.544
Taking a detour.


01:01:41.676 --> 01:01:44.549
We're gonna take a little trip
down memory lane.


01:02:11.271 --> 01:02:13.665
This was my home
for eight and a half years.


01:02:13.708 --> 01:02:16.233
Since we were near,
I thought we'd drop by.


01:02:19.018 --> 01:02:21.020
Up there, second floor.


01:02:21.063 --> 01:02:22.978
202 B Pod.


01:02:24.545 --> 01:02:27.722
I got my own place
after the first year.


01:02:27.766 --> 01:02:29.942
Then, um...


01:02:29.985 --> 01:02:32.640
another place
on the other side.


01:02:34.294 --> 01:02:35.991
You know that fella
I told you about,


01:02:36.035 --> 01:02:37.689
the one I wanted you to meet?


01:02:37.732 --> 01:02:39.560
He's here.


01:02:39.604 --> 01:02:41.867
Thought I'd pay him a visit.
I've arranged it.


01:02:41.910 --> 01:02:43.869
Want to join?


01:02:45.262 --> 01:02:46.872
Go into a military prison?


01:02:46.915 --> 01:02:48.569
No. No, thanks.


01:02:48.613 --> 01:02:50.441
Well, it's pretty good
as far as prisons go.


01:02:50.484 --> 01:02:53.313
You know, built in 2002.


01:02:53.357 --> 01:02:56.273
Things still work, like toilets.


01:02:56.316 --> 01:02:58.753
Shit, man, I mean,
you walk in there


01:02:58.797 --> 01:03:00.973
and those doors close
behind you, that's fucking it.


01:03:01.016 --> 01:03:02.453
I'm going in.


01:03:02.496 --> 01:03:04.324
Come on.
Think of it as a field trip.


01:03:04.368 --> 01:03:07.153
As a teachable moment.


01:03:07.196 --> 01:03:09.068
I'll wait in the car.


01:03:11.418 --> 01:03:13.377
I'm inviting you.


01:03:15.683 --> 01:03:17.598
I ain't going.


01:03:23.125 --> 01:03:24.823
Just park the car.


01:04:00.598 --> 01:04:02.817
Hey, you ever been
on Google Earth?


01:04:04.906 --> 01:04:06.691
What is that?


01:04:06.734 --> 01:04:09.041
It's where I was when I was
waiting for you. It's amazing.


01:04:09.084 --> 01:04:10.869
Look, you can enter any place
in the world.


01:04:10.912 --> 01:04:12.827
It comes right up.
Street View.


01:04:12.871 --> 01:04:14.829
Look at that.
290 Great Hills Road.


01:04:14.873 --> 01:04:16.527
Rockville, Virginia.


01:04:16.570 --> 01:04:19.138
The house, the surroundings,
latitude, longitude.


01:04:19.181 --> 01:04:21.314
That's John Gordo's house.


01:04:22.968 --> 01:04:25.927
Front entrance, back entrance.


01:04:27.451 --> 01:04:30.410
You still got him on the brain?


01:04:30.454 --> 01:04:32.107
Yes, sir.


01:04:34.022 --> 01:04:36.721
I don't think that's
such a great idea.


01:04:47.079 --> 01:04:49.168
How'd it go at Leavenworth?


01:04:55.740 --> 01:04:57.655
You still pissed at me?


01:05:01.485 --> 01:05:03.443
Hey, wasn't La Linda
supposed to meet us here?


01:05:03.487 --> 01:05:04.923
Yeah.


01:05:04.966 --> 01:05:06.794
She'll be here tomorrow.


01:05:06.838 --> 01:05:08.796
Meet us in Saint Louis,


01:05:08.840 --> 01:05:11.582
then do a deep stacks
in Biloxi.


01:05:11.625 --> 01:05:14.846
Tunica, and on to Panama City.


01:05:16.413 --> 01:05:18.153
You like her, huh?


01:05:22.984 --> 01:05:25.073
Yeah.


01:05:25.117 --> 01:05:26.945
Yeah. Me, too.


01:05:28.773 --> 01:05:30.818
You ever been married?


01:05:36.302 --> 01:05:39.523
When I was in the service,
I was a bit of a ladies' man.


01:05:39.566 --> 01:05:41.263
Thought I was.


01:05:41.307 --> 01:05:43.875
But, uh...


01:05:43.918 --> 01:05:46.486
then the other stuff happened.


01:05:46.530 --> 01:05:48.836
The narrative was broken.


01:05:51.796 --> 01:05:54.102
So, how long's it been
since you got laid?


01:05:59.151 --> 01:06:01.719
How long has it been
since you've seen your mother?


01:06:01.762 --> 01:06:03.590
I wouldn't know
where to find her.


01:06:03.634 --> 01:06:05.505
That's bullshit.


01:06:05.549 --> 01:06:07.681
What business is it
of yours, anyway?


01:06:08.682 --> 01:06:11.206
-You remember her?
-Sure.


01:06:11.250 --> 01:06:14.166
Yeah? She reach out to you?


01:06:14.209 --> 01:06:16.255
She try and contact you?


01:06:18.866 --> 01:06:21.565
I'll make you a deal, Kid.


01:06:21.608 --> 01:06:24.524
You go see your mother,
and I'll fucking get laid.


01:06:32.793 --> 01:06:35.622
About earlier:
I don't like prisons.


01:06:36.928 --> 01:06:38.669
Even seeing them
on the highway here,


01:06:38.712 --> 01:06:42.368
looking at it and...
you realize,


01:06:42.411 --> 01:06:44.544
"Oh, my God, that's a prison."


01:06:47.852 --> 01:06:50.855
My dad used to send my mom
letters from Bagram,


01:06:50.898 --> 01:06:53.205
and she'd cry.


01:07:02.780 --> 01:07:05.260
There's something
quite similar in poker.


01:07:06.305 --> 01:07:08.089
You know the phrase "tilt"?


01:07:08.133 --> 01:07:09.613
Yeah.


01:07:09.656 --> 01:07:11.440
When a player gets
caught up in winning,


01:07:11.484 --> 01:07:13.878
plays outside his zone.


01:07:13.921 --> 01:07:16.184
Just like in pinball.


01:07:18.622 --> 01:07:21.538
And there's something similar
in interrogations.


01:07:21.581 --> 01:07:23.931
It's called "force drift."


01:07:23.975 --> 01:07:27.282
It happens when
the interrogator applies


01:07:27.326 --> 01:07:30.808
more and more force to
the prisoner with less results.


01:07:32.418 --> 01:07:34.463
The interrogator
becomes intoxicated


01:07:34.507 --> 01:07:36.857
by frustration and power.


01:07:38.685 --> 01:07:41.383
Any man can tilt.


01:07:41.427 --> 01:07:43.777
I can tilt.


01:07:43.821 --> 01:07:45.910
Your father can tilt.


01:07:47.302 --> 01:07:49.435
You can tilt.


01:07:55.136 --> 01:07:57.312
I said ride with me.


01:07:57.356 --> 01:07:59.488
You did.


01:07:59.532 --> 01:08:01.578
You came along.


01:08:03.536 --> 01:08:06.583
What do you think we're up to,
you and me?


01:08:56.676 --> 01:08:59.200
-La Linda!


01:09:01.638 --> 01:09:03.988
Here, I preregistered you
with a buy-in.


01:09:04.031 --> 01:09:06.947
Now, your name is getting
some recognition value.


01:09:06.991 --> 01:09:08.949
Well, that's always
a good thing.


01:09:08.993 --> 01:09:11.038
-How's the turnout?


01:09:11.082 --> 01:09:13.650
-Uh, it's normal.
-Oh.


01:09:13.693 --> 01:09:15.913
You know that guy, uh,
that's always doing like this?


01:09:15.956 --> 01:09:18.437
-Religious Ronnie.
-Yeah. He's here.


01:09:18.480 --> 01:09:20.744
Got the Santa Tanita
and all that stuff with him.


01:09:20.787 --> 01:09:22.920
-Santeria.
-Santeria...


01:09:26.924 --> 01:09:28.490
-Mm, mm, mm.


01:10:23.328 --> 01:10:25.722
Let's get the cards in the air!


01:10:52.966 --> 01:10:54.402
Clock!


01:10:54.446 --> 01:10:56.143
Clock on 38.


01:10:59.277 --> 01:11:00.800
Okay, okay.


01:11:00.844 --> 01:11:02.062
A great player can see


01:11:02.106 --> 01:11:04.325
right into your soul.


01:11:04.369 --> 01:11:06.806
He can wear earplugs,


01:11:06.850 --> 01:11:10.288
a hoodie, a baseball cap,


01:11:10.331 --> 01:11:14.205
mirrored glasses, a ski mask,


01:11:14.248 --> 01:11:16.511
but he'll see right
into your soul.


01:11:16.555 --> 01:11:18.122
Call.


01:11:28.828 --> 01:11:30.830
-Where's Cirk?
-He must have crashed.


01:11:30.874 --> 01:11:32.701
I'll call him and wake him up.


01:11:32.745 --> 01:11:34.878
No, that's all right.
Don't bother.


01:11:34.921 --> 01:11:36.662
I want a drink.


01:11:36.705 --> 01:11:38.533
What can I get you-all?


01:11:38.577 --> 01:11:40.013
Uh, I'll have a Tanqueray
on the rocks.


01:11:40.057 --> 01:11:42.668
I'll have a Jack, uh,


01:11:42.711 --> 01:11:44.583
double, neat.


01:11:46.193 --> 01:11:47.629
You talk to him.


01:11:47.673 --> 01:11:49.631
Have you noticed anything
about him lately?


01:11:49.675 --> 01:11:51.982
Like what?


01:11:52.025 --> 01:11:53.984
Moody and...


01:11:54.027 --> 01:11:56.551
I don't... I don't know.


01:11:56.595 --> 01:11:59.685
Well, I got a offer for
a sponsorship from Rock Poker.


01:11:59.728 --> 01:12:01.382
10,000, for you.


01:12:01.426 --> 01:12:03.515
Yeah?
That's the one with the, uh,


01:12:03.558 --> 01:12:05.473
little pony logo
on the titty, right?


01:12:05.517 --> 01:12:07.649
Yeah, the rocking horse
with the word "poker."


01:12:09.477 --> 01:12:12.785
Are you all right?


01:12:12.829 --> 01:12:15.744
Yeah. I'm fucking all right.


01:12:15.788 --> 01:12:17.355
"Fucking all right."


01:12:17.398 --> 01:12:20.314
Crying and shit.


01:12:20.358 --> 01:12:22.621
-What do I have to do
for this sponsorship? -Mm.


01:12:22.664 --> 01:12:24.318
You just have to wear
their T-shirts


01:12:24.362 --> 01:12:26.103
during the tournaments.


01:12:27.495 --> 01:12:29.454
I-I had to ask.


01:12:29.497 --> 01:12:31.412
It was an offer.


01:12:33.762 --> 01:12:35.547
I wish the Kid had been here.


01:12:35.590 --> 01:12:37.723
-Well, let me call him.
-No, it's all right.


01:12:37.766 --> 01:12:39.420
Leave him alone.


01:12:43.511 --> 01:12:46.253
You know you made the cut.
This is your moment.


01:12:48.255 --> 01:12:52.607
You know, I think that you have
the wrong idea about me.


01:12:52.651 --> 01:12:55.349
Yes, I-I want to win the money.


01:12:55.393 --> 01:12:57.177
I want to go
to the World Series,


01:12:57.221 --> 01:13:00.224
but then that's it.


01:13:00.267 --> 01:13:04.445
This kid Cirk, he needs help.


01:13:04.489 --> 01:13:06.534
He's got financial debts.


01:13:07.796 --> 01:13:09.407
And I understand him.


01:13:09.450 --> 01:13:11.322
And if I can help him,


01:13:11.365 --> 01:13:13.933
maybe he has a chance
to start over again,


01:13:13.977 --> 01:13:17.154
resume his education
and start a life.


01:13:17.197 --> 01:13:20.331
-And you would do all that?


01:13:20.374 --> 01:13:22.115
Well...


01:13:22.159 --> 01:13:23.769
yeah.


01:13:24.726 --> 01:13:26.380
Yeah.


01:13:26.424 --> 01:13:28.948
You have to be the strangest
poker player I ever met.


01:13:28.992 --> 01:13:31.777
-Oh, you have no idea.
-Mm.


01:13:33.561 --> 01:13:36.086
What you doing tomorrow?
You're off.


01:13:39.393 --> 01:13:41.961
I got no plans.


01:13:42.005 --> 01:13:44.355
She said to me,


01:13:44.398 --> 01:13:46.966
"Did you ever see a city
all lit up at night?"


01:13:49.273 --> 01:13:52.406
I said, "Yeah, I've seen
a whole city on fire."


01:13:55.844 --> 01:13:58.630
"Not like that," she said.


01:14:10.163 --> 01:14:11.556
Bobby, you must see this.


01:14:11.599 --> 01:14:13.123
I didn't have it bad.


01:14:13.166 --> 01:14:14.689
Come on, trust me.
This is amazing.


01:14:14.733 --> 01:14:16.561
That's not what I meant to say.


01:14:16.604 --> 01:14:18.737
Of course you know
other people have it better.


01:14:18.780 --> 01:14:21.914
And you learn to be careful
around certain people.


01:14:21.958 --> 01:14:25.657
But I had friends,
and I had family, of course.


01:14:25.700 --> 01:14:27.093
They had a park.


01:14:27.137 --> 01:14:28.834
They lit it up like this.


01:14:28.877 --> 01:14:31.402
Much bigger.


01:14:31.445 --> 01:14:33.099
How would I know?


01:14:33.143 --> 01:14:34.709
I was just a little kid.


01:14:34.753 --> 01:14:36.233
Everything was bigger.


01:14:36.276 --> 01:14:38.713
-This was Saint Louis?
-Yeah.


01:14:42.152 --> 01:14:43.936
You know,
it doesn't matter to me


01:14:43.980 --> 01:14:46.373
if you did something bad
in the past.


01:14:46.417 --> 01:14:48.419
You can tell me about it.


01:14:52.075 --> 01:14:53.990
Yeah, I don't know.


01:14:56.905 --> 01:14:59.082
What could be so bad?


01:15:02.737 --> 01:15:04.522
I was just a kid.


01:15:04.565 --> 01:15:06.437
Everything was bigger.


01:15:06.480 --> 01:15:08.134
Just in your mind.


01:15:48.522 --> 01:15:50.916
I'm glad you suggested
this place.


01:17:17.872 --> 01:17:21.311
No! In the name
of Jesus and Mary,


01:17:21.354 --> 01:17:23.051
what have you done to me?


01:17:23.095 --> 01:17:25.358
I have done nothing to you!


01:17:27.491 --> 01:17:29.667
USA! USA!


01:17:29.710 --> 01:17:33.714
USA! USA! USA!


01:17:52.994 --> 01:17:54.474
Call.


01:19:22.606 --> 01:19:24.303
Hey.


01:19:26.523 --> 01:19:28.133
Where were you?


01:19:28.176 --> 01:19:30.048
Oh, played a little blackjack.


01:19:30.091 --> 01:19:31.876
How'd that go?


01:19:31.919 --> 01:19:33.791
Came out ahead.


01:19:33.834 --> 01:19:35.532
Nice.


01:19:40.667 --> 01:19:43.322
How do you like it?


01:19:43.366 --> 01:19:45.063
-Like what?
-This.


01:19:45.106 --> 01:19:46.760
This life...


01:19:46.804 --> 01:19:48.849
we have, you and me.


01:19:50.155 --> 01:19:52.113
Yeah. It's cool.


01:19:52.157 --> 01:19:54.551
That's for sure, but...


01:19:54.594 --> 01:19:56.683
But what?


01:19:58.946 --> 01:20:01.645
It's all the same.


01:20:01.688 --> 01:20:05.431
You know, it's...
it's repetitive.


01:20:05.475 --> 01:20:07.303
It's, uh...


01:20:07.346 --> 01:20:11.394
I don't know if it really feels
like it's going anywhere.


01:20:13.613 --> 01:20:17.922
Well, you know, you just go
around and around


01:20:17.965 --> 01:20:20.011
until you work things out.


01:20:22.274 --> 01:20:24.320
How's that going for you?


01:20:28.236 --> 01:20:30.369
You given it any more thought?


01:20:35.200 --> 01:20:36.854
No.


01:20:42.120 --> 01:20:45.253
You going to
the World Series of Poker?


01:20:45.297 --> 01:20:47.038
Already registered.


01:20:47.081 --> 01:20:48.387
That'll be cool.


01:20:48.431 --> 01:20:50.520
Yeah, that'll be it for me.


01:20:50.563 --> 01:20:53.044
You gonna quit?
Quit the circuit?


01:20:55.176 --> 01:20:57.222
I've done my time.


01:20:59.311 --> 01:21:00.747
Look...


01:21:02.009 --> 01:21:04.055
I don't know if...


01:21:04.098 --> 01:21:06.797
I'm up for going to Vegas.


01:21:09.103 --> 01:21:11.584
Yeah? You gonna bail?


01:21:32.736 --> 01:21:34.825
It's late,
but you got a second?


01:21:37.305 --> 01:21:39.264
Sure.


01:21:40.308 --> 01:21:42.485
I want to show you something.


01:21:42.528 --> 01:21:44.661
You have a moment?


01:21:44.704 --> 01:21:46.402
I got a proposal.


01:21:47.446 --> 01:21:49.317
Come here. Follow me.


01:22:22.916 --> 01:22:24.570
Come on.


01:22:44.329 --> 01:22:46.026
You live like this?


01:22:46.070 --> 01:22:47.854
Sit down.


01:22:55.949 --> 01:22:57.821
Need anything?


01:22:57.864 --> 01:22:59.736
Some water?


01:22:59.779 --> 01:23:01.694
No, I'm fine.


01:23:04.131 --> 01:23:06.220
How about...


01:23:06.264 --> 01:23:09.136
a sandbag
to put over your head?


01:23:11.878 --> 01:23:13.924
They sell them on eBay.


01:23:16.927 --> 01:23:19.016
When civilian contractor
John Gordo


01:23:19.059 --> 01:23:21.192
first approached me
in Abu Ghraib,


01:23:21.235 --> 01:23:23.499
he said I needed
to be more creative.


01:23:23.542 --> 01:23:28.199
He said I had talent
but I lacked imagination.


01:23:28.242 --> 01:23:29.722
Would you agree with that?


01:23:29.766 --> 01:23:31.811
Bill, what the fuck
is going on here?


01:23:31.855 --> 01:23:33.813
Real life is going on.


01:23:35.249 --> 01:23:37.034
World Series of Torture.


01:23:37.077 --> 01:23:39.384
-I'm gonna sp...
-Stay seated!


01:23:40.994 --> 01:23:43.301
You sure I can't get you
any water?


01:23:45.390 --> 01:23:47.871
You may wish
you had accepted later.


01:23:51.614 --> 01:23:54.225
Do I have
your attention now, Cirk?


01:23:55.574 --> 01:23:58.272
Do I? Do I?!


01:23:59.360 --> 01:24:01.101
Yeah.


01:24:01.145 --> 01:24:02.755
Good.


01:24:04.714 --> 01:24:09.501
Are the little nerves at the
ends of your fingers and toes


01:24:09.545 --> 01:24:13.113
and the tip of your dick
starting to tingle with fear?


01:24:17.378 --> 01:24:19.163
Good.


01:24:19.206 --> 01:24:21.295
Let me enhance this
a little bit.


01:24:35.353 --> 01:24:37.529
I've been doing a little
investigating about you,


01:24:37.573 --> 01:24:39.879
Cirk with a "C."


01:24:41.272 --> 01:24:43.753
About your father--
I did meet him at Abu Ghraib.


01:24:43.796 --> 01:24:45.537
I lied about that.


01:24:45.581 --> 01:24:49.106
Your mother,
your time in college,


01:24:49.149 --> 01:24:50.847
your scrapes with the law.


01:24:50.890 --> 01:24:53.197
It's all on the Internet,
of course.


01:24:55.895 --> 01:24:58.245
I'm gonna make you a proposal.


01:25:01.814 --> 01:25:03.294
Sit up.


01:25:11.041 --> 01:25:16.829
You have approximately $20,000
in college loan debts.


01:25:23.749 --> 01:25:25.621
20,000.


01:25:27.013 --> 01:25:28.711
To go back to college--


01:25:28.754 --> 01:25:32.366
tuition, expenses,
condoms and so forth--


01:25:32.410 --> 01:25:35.848
it adds up,
so let's say another...


01:25:38.329 --> 01:25:40.244
...80,000.


01:25:42.855 --> 01:25:46.859
On top of that, you've got
$5,000 in credit card debt.


01:25:46.903 --> 01:25:49.383
Your mama-- bless her,
she's got her problems--


01:25:49.427 --> 01:25:52.473
she's about 35 grand
underwater,


01:25:52.517 --> 01:25:56.042
with the mortgage and all,
so let's say 40 grand.


01:25:56.086 --> 01:25:58.001
And for the heck of it,
let's throw in


01:25:58.044 --> 01:25:59.698
another ten grand pocket money.


01:25:59.742 --> 01:26:04.094
That's 150 grand, cash,
tax free.


01:26:04.137 --> 01:26:06.966
All that's yours
on one condition.


01:26:07.010 --> 01:26:08.925
And what is that?


01:26:21.241 --> 01:26:24.680
Go see your mother.


01:26:30.773 --> 01:26:33.863
She lives
in Fall River, Oregon.


01:26:33.906 --> 01:26:35.516
I have the address.


01:26:35.560 --> 01:26:36.909
I spoke to her.


01:26:36.953 --> 01:26:39.303
I didn't tell her
who I was, of course.


01:26:39.346 --> 01:26:42.045
Go visit her.


01:26:42.088 --> 01:26:44.003
Forgive her.


01:26:44.047 --> 01:26:45.788
Make things right with her.


01:26:45.831 --> 01:26:47.659
Clear up her debt.


01:26:47.703 --> 01:26:50.662
Tell her about
your college plans.


01:26:50.706 --> 01:26:53.143
Then put her on the phone
with me.


01:26:54.579 --> 01:26:57.364
I want to hear her say
these things.


01:26:57.408 --> 01:26:59.497
I want to hear her voice.


01:27:08.767 --> 01:27:10.682
You serious?


01:27:13.076 --> 01:27:14.730
Yes.


01:27:20.518 --> 01:27:22.738
And if I don't?


01:27:25.305 --> 01:27:28.395
This is not a proposal
you can afford to reject.


01:27:30.615 --> 01:27:33.096
And if you cheat me,


01:27:33.139 --> 01:27:35.141
I'll find you.


01:27:36.490 --> 01:27:38.536
You don't want that to happen.


01:27:42.714 --> 01:27:45.412
I don't like celebrity gambling.


01:27:46.631 --> 01:27:49.068
I like anonymous gambling.


01:27:49.112 --> 01:27:51.070
I did this for you.


01:27:52.724 --> 01:27:54.770
You hear what I'm saying?


01:28:03.735 --> 01:28:05.606
Yeah.


01:28:06.651 --> 01:28:08.435
Do we have a deal?


01:28:13.876 --> 01:28:15.791
Yeah, we have a deal.


01:28:17.140 --> 01:28:19.533
Thank you.


01:28:19.577 --> 01:28:21.361
Okay.


01:28:21.405 --> 01:28:22.972
Let's give her a call.


01:28:23.015 --> 01:28:25.844
She'll still be up right now.


01:28:25.888 --> 01:28:27.585
Yeah.


01:29:02.228 --> 01:29:04.056
One sec!


01:29:05.144 --> 01:29:06.537
Who is it?


01:29:06.580 --> 01:29:08.321
It's William.


01:29:11.150 --> 01:29:13.065
What's up? Thought we were
meeting in the pit.


01:29:13.109 --> 01:29:14.545
-You cool?
-Yeah.


01:29:14.588 --> 01:29:16.373
Yeah.


01:29:16.416 --> 01:29:18.592
Uh, we got final table
tomorrow.


01:29:18.636 --> 01:29:20.507
Yeah, no, I know.
30, right?


01:29:20.551 --> 01:29:22.335
Hey, where's your sidekick?


01:29:22.379 --> 01:29:24.903
Oh, yeah, he had to...
he had to go home.


01:29:24.947 --> 01:29:26.818
His mom's not feeling well.


01:29:26.862 --> 01:29:28.515
-He has a mom?
-Yeah.


01:29:28.559 --> 01:29:29.995
Believe it or not.


01:29:30.039 --> 01:29:31.779
So, what's on your mind?


01:29:31.823 --> 01:29:33.477
Um...


01:29:34.695 --> 01:29:39.048
I made a promise to Cirk
before I left.


01:29:39.091 --> 01:29:41.267
You know, he talks about you.
He fancies you.


01:29:41.311 --> 01:29:44.488
You mean he
fancies himself a matchmaker.


01:29:46.403 --> 01:29:49.841
I promised him that I'd...


01:29:49.885 --> 01:29:53.192
act on these feelings I have.


01:29:54.585 --> 01:29:57.370
These feelings towards you.


01:29:57.414 --> 01:29:58.806
Oh.


01:29:58.850 --> 01:30:01.200
I think you may have them, too.


01:30:09.600 --> 01:30:11.210
You do, huh?


01:30:11.254 --> 01:30:12.995
Yes, I do.


01:30:27.313 --> 01:30:29.054
The feeling of being


01:30:29.098 --> 01:30:32.840
forgiven by another
and forgiving oneself


01:30:32.884 --> 01:30:34.930
are so much alike...


01:30:37.019 --> 01:30:40.022
...there's no point in trying
to keep them distinct.


01:30:44.504 --> 01:30:46.376
How much time we got?


01:30:47.420 --> 01:30:49.292
Come look at this.


01:30:51.381 --> 01:30:53.035
What?


01:30:54.514 --> 01:30:56.299
JUDY
Cirk?


01:30:56.342 --> 01:30:58.127
My God, Cirk, is that you?


01:30:58.170 --> 01:31:00.129
-Yeah, Mom. Yeah, Mom, it's me.
-What? Where are you?


01:31:00.172 --> 01:31:02.261
I'm in Panama City.


01:31:02.305 --> 01:31:03.871
Well, what's happening?


01:31:03.915 --> 01:31:05.873
It-it's been so long.


01:31:05.917 --> 01:31:09.094
Mom, I've been thinking, and...


01:31:09.138 --> 01:31:11.618
I haven't been fair to you.


01:31:11.662 --> 01:31:13.620
I want to come and see you.


01:31:15.361 --> 01:31:17.363
Are you... are you all right?


01:31:17.407 --> 01:31:18.843
So it goes on
like that for a while.


01:31:18.886 --> 01:31:20.323
Got a little maudlin.


01:31:20.366 --> 01:31:22.064
She lives outside of Portland.


01:31:22.107 --> 01:31:23.848
He'll be there in a day or two.


01:31:23.891 --> 01:31:26.068
-He'll call me from there.
-Mm.


01:31:26.111 --> 01:31:28.592
How'd you get him to do that?


01:31:28.635 --> 01:31:30.681
He wanted to.


01:31:30.724 --> 01:31:33.118
Just needed an excuse.


01:31:33.162 --> 01:31:34.772
I may go visit them.


01:31:34.815 --> 01:31:37.818
I never played the Northwest.


01:31:37.862 --> 01:31:40.691
And welcome to the final table.


01:31:49.178 --> 01:31:50.744
You keep tabs on this.


01:31:50.788 --> 01:31:52.877
-I'm expecting a call.
-Mm-hmm.


01:32:22.950 --> 01:32:25.170
-MR.Yes!


01:32:25.214 --> 01:32:27.694
USA! USA!


01:32:27.738 --> 01:32:29.609
USA!


01:32:38.531 --> 01:32:40.403
Well done.


01:32:45.799 --> 01:32:47.540
All right, players.


01:32:47.584 --> 01:32:49.107
That's the end of the level.


01:32:49.151 --> 01:32:51.109
90-minute dinner break.


01:32:57.985 --> 01:33:00.075
Your phone was buzzing.


01:33:05.689 --> 01:33:07.604
It's from Cirk.


01:33:07.647 --> 01:33:10.085
-"Wish you were here."


01:33:17.396 --> 01:33:19.572
Nice.


01:33:19.616 --> 01:33:21.661
You got about ten minutes.


01:34:39.522 --> 01:34:41.437
Good game.


01:34:41.480 --> 01:34:43.134
Good game, man.


01:36:07.827 --> 01:36:09.264
I need a minute.


01:36:18.011 --> 01:36:19.709
What's going on?


01:36:21.711 --> 01:36:23.539
Floor.


01:36:32.330 --> 01:36:34.332
Thanks for joining me
here in Rockville, Virginia.


01:36:34.376 --> 01:36:36.334
Ryan Choi
with Eleven Alive News.


01:36:36.378 --> 01:36:39.424
We are currently on the scene
of Major John Gordo's home.


01:36:39.468 --> 01:36:41.208
Now, what we do know is that


01:36:41.252 --> 01:36:43.298
there has been
a unidentified suspect


01:36:43.341 --> 01:36:46.170
that was armed
with a pellet pistol.


01:36:46.213 --> 01:36:48.781
The suspect fired and missed.


01:36:48.825 --> 01:36:52.089
Major Gordo returned fire,
killing the suspect.


01:36:52.132 --> 01:36:54.874
Earlier today,
I spoke with Major Gordo.


01:36:54.918 --> 01:36:56.615
You purchase security


01:36:56.659 --> 01:36:58.530
thinking something like this
might happen,


01:36:58.574 --> 01:37:01.490
but you don't think
it ever will.


01:37:01.533 --> 01:37:04.362
In other news, a fire
in the warehouse district


01:37:04.406 --> 01:37:06.712
of suspicious origin.


01:37:06.756 --> 01:37:08.845
Four fire companies responded.


01:37:08.888 --> 01:37:10.586
There were no
reported injuries,


01:37:10.629 --> 01:37:12.457
and the fire was brought
under control


01:37:12.501 --> 01:37:15.373
after roughly 90 minutes.


01:37:15.417 --> 01:37:18.637
Fire investigators
are on the scene.


01:39:39.735 --> 01:39:41.998
It's turned off.


01:39:55.925 --> 01:39:57.883
Come sit down, John.


01:39:59.058 --> 01:40:00.930
Don't be stupid.


01:40:24.997 --> 01:40:26.695
You remember me?


01:40:26.738 --> 01:40:28.479
Should I?


01:40:30.699 --> 01:40:33.092
Tier 1A, Abu Ghraib.


01:40:35.704 --> 01:40:37.401
Tillich?


01:40:38.620 --> 01:40:40.447
Bill Tillich.


01:40:42.972 --> 01:40:46.192
You look pretty good,
all things considered.


01:40:48.630 --> 01:40:50.588
How long were you
in Leavenworth?


01:40:50.632 --> 01:40:53.156
-Eight and a half years.
-That's a bitch.


01:40:59.510 --> 01:41:02.252
That boy that you shot...


01:41:03.949 --> 01:41:06.125
...he wanted to kill you.


01:41:06.169 --> 01:41:07.910
I assumed that.


01:41:09.912 --> 01:41:12.871
You trained his father--


01:41:12.915 --> 01:41:15.482
his name was Roger Baufort--


01:41:15.526 --> 01:41:17.572
just like you trained me.


01:41:19.008 --> 01:41:21.663
What happened to him?


01:41:21.706 --> 01:41:23.708
He shot himself.


01:41:25.667 --> 01:41:28.147
So I'm to blame?


01:41:28.191 --> 01:41:31.237
That's a pussified defense,
PFC Tillich,


01:41:31.281 --> 01:41:33.196
and you know it.


01:41:33.239 --> 01:41:36.721
We are each responsible
for our own actions.


01:41:40.072 --> 01:41:42.118
I believe that.


01:41:44.860 --> 01:41:48.211
We are going to go
into the next room,


01:41:48.254 --> 01:41:50.300
you and I...


01:41:51.867 --> 01:41:54.652
...and we are going to have
a dramatic reenactment.


01:41:57.524 --> 01:42:00.092
Only one of us
will come out alive.


01:42:02.704 --> 01:42:04.880
I'm going to make things right.


01:42:06.969 --> 01:42:09.667
Either that, John Rodgers...


01:42:11.713 --> 01:42:13.671
...or I'm going to blast
a bullet


01:42:13.715 --> 01:42:15.804
straight through your eyeball.


01:42:33.386 --> 01:42:35.084
Lead the way.


01:42:35.127 --> 01:42:36.955
After you.


01:42:46.704 --> 01:42:48.837
I got some cigarettes.
Do you want one?


01:42:48.880 --> 01:42:50.795
No.


01:42:50.839 --> 01:42:53.319
Neither do I.


01:42:53.363 --> 01:42:55.278
Who goes first?


01:42:56.758 --> 01:42:58.455
Me.


01:44:03.433 --> 01:44:05.522
Emergency services?


01:44:08.307 --> 01:44:10.440
I'd like to report a homicide.


01:44:12.659 --> 01:44:14.923
290 Great Falls Road.


01:44:51.002 --> 01:44:52.656
I never imagined myself


01:44:52.699 --> 01:44:55.746
as someone suited
to a life of incarceration.


01:44:59.837 --> 01:45:01.404
Inmate Tillich.


01:45:01.447 --> 01:45:03.101
You got a visitor.

